  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mother School Society</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&#x2019;other School Society will support women working in Israeli settlements to build their self-confidence, enhance their awareness of their legal rights, and provide them with alternative opportunities which would support them to stop working in the Israelisettlements. The project will also shed light and enhance the awareness of communities and key stakeholders and actors on women&#x2019;s rights violations in Israeli settlements to contribute to advocacy work and provide economic alternatives as part of the broader solution at the policy level.
 Mother School Society will work to enhance the social and economic empowerment of Palestinian women working in Israeli settlements. This overall objective will be achieved through:
- Palestinian women working in Israeli settlements are empowered by reinforcing their mental health, self-esteem and increased awareness of legal and human rights violations in the workplace.
- Palestinian women working in Israeli settlements have improved. knowledge and capacities to manage and develop alternative income-generating activities.
- The Palestinian Authority and other national stakeholders have enhanced knowledge and awareness about the rights violations experienced by Palestinian women working in Israeli settlements.</narrative>
  </description>
